But how many turns do your games generally last?  The
pseudo-randomness that NetHack uses ensures that luck will
fundamentally balance out over the course of a game; if you survive
long enough, the chance of you encountering "good luck" increases.

I don't think I've had good games because I've had good luck; I think
I've had good luck because I've used good strategy to make sure I
survive long enough to have it.

And I think this because the overwhelming trend in my NH games has
been that I consitently get better at it.  If luck was the primary
factor for survival, Marvin wouldn't ascend 22 of 25 games and my top
100 list wouldn't contain only characters that scored over 10,000
points.

